 "otherWalls": "window-grid",
 "palette": {
  "brick": "#3f322d",
  "frame": "#b5a68a",
  "door": "#a85a34",
  "stone": "#5a4c44"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Kit batch 2005+ (lane kit-batch-2005-20261121), hand-authored. One system on every street front, written as per-house components: raised brick bays (4 bays: two pairs of slot windows on storeys 1-3, two windows in the brick top storey, two front doors) alternating with French-window bays (one or two two-light French windows per storey, a zinc mansard storey with one dormer per bay, wide ground windows). Five storeys: a 3.5 m banded brick ground and four 3.1 m storeys, the top one zinc between the brick bays.",
